{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>I have not eaten in my oni.</b> Like בן אוני (son of my mourning) and לחם אונים (bread of mourning). I have hinted at the reason regarding the sacred language; the meaning of oni is like 'my mourning,' for if I were a mourner I would not have eaten. [Some say: sacred.] From the tithe." "<b>Nor have I removed from it.</b> The meaning: I have not corrupted [anything] from the sacred portion." "<b>In impurity.</b> In an impure thing." "<b>For the dead.</b> For the needs of the dead. And some say: for idol worship. And the meaning of 'in these things' is that it is forbidden to remove from the grain for any purpose until giving the tithe, which is sacred — for if he gives from the permitted portion, it is a way of contempt. And even if he gave in impurity. And just as I guarded myself and guarded the grain in order to bring out the sacred portion, so may our Elohim guard our land — and this is the meaning of 'and the land.'"], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {0 "The bracketed [ס״א קודש] indicates a variant reading: one witness reads קודש (sacred) instead of קודם (before). The clause's syntax is compressed; Ibn Ezra appears to cite the variant as substituting 'sacred' for 'before' in the phrase."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:24:58.726383970Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}